course: dictionary
lesson: 10825
title: A word from the grasslands
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words are new, but the sentences around them give you clues. «Long ago the Leopard lived on the bare, hot, sandy High Veldt.» The words bare and hot tell you the veldt has little shade or greenery, and «the empty veldt» tells you not much is growing there. So the veldt is a wide, open place with few trees.
explain: Compare it with the forest the animals move to: «a forest full of stripy, speckly, patchy-blatchy shadows». Shadows come from trees, so the forest has many trees and the veldt has few. Ask yourself what word would fit in the sentence. Grassland fits, so it is a good guess, and the dictionary confirms it.
explain: Context can also show colour. The Leopard was «exactly the same sandy-yellow-brown as the ground», so he could hide by a stone. The clues tell you the veldt is sandy and yellow-brown, not green and leafy. Each clue adds a little more to the picture.
explain: Some words come from other languages. Veld comes from Afrikaans and Dutch, where it means field. When context is not enough, a dictionary settles it, and here the dictionary tells you the veldt is the wide, open grassland of southern Africa.
fact: Veldt means the wide, open grassland of southern Africa.
fact: Veld is another spelling of veldt, and it comes from Afrikaans and Dutch, where it means «field».
fact: The veldt has few trees, and animals like zebras, giraffes and antelope live there.
fact: In South Africa, the veld has a high veld and a low veld, so there is more than one kind of grassland.
fact: In «How the Leopard Got His Spots», the High Veldt is sandy-yellow, while the forest is full of «stripy, speckly, patchy-blatchy shadows».
exercise: «Long ago the Leopard lived on the bare, hot, sandy High Veldt.» What kind of place is the veldt? | A dark forest full of shadows | *Wide, open grassland with few trees | A cold mountain covered in snow | A deep river with fish in it
exercise: The animals leave the veldt for «a forest full of stripy, speckly, patchy-blatchy shadows». What is the main difference between the two places? | The veldt has more shadows than the forest | Both places are cold and wet | *The forest has many trees, and the veldt has few | The forest is sandy and the veldt is green
exercise: The word veld comes from Afrikaans and Dutch. What does it mean in those languages? | Mountain | *Field | Forest | River
test: «The Leopard was exactly the same sandy-yellow-brown as the ground.» Why could he hide so well on the veldt? | He had a loud roar to scare the others | *He matched the sandy yellow-brown colour of the ground | He was hiding in a dark forest | He was the same colour as the sandy ground
test: Where would you most likely find zebras and giraffes living in the wild, according to the dictionary? | *The wide, open grassland of southern Africa | A busy city street | A cold, snowy mountain | A deep, dark forest
exam: Which of these is the best clue that the veldt is an open place with few trees? | The Leopard lived on the bare, hot, sandy High Veldt | *The veldt is described as the empty, wide, open grassland | The Giraffe had the longest legs | The Baboon gave the animals riddles
